# econ-paper-studio

When the user is working on an empirical economics paper or asks for econometric/paper-writing help:

1. Read `AGENTS.md`, `SKILL.md`, `skill_loadout.yaml`, `research_skill_registry.yaml`, `docs/UPSTREAM_SKILLS.md`, and `docs/AGENT_RUNBOOK.md`.
2. Treat this as an agent-native workflow. Load or read upstream skills before substantive econometrics, writing, or citation work.
3. Run `econ-studio skills plan --task full-paper` and audit third-party skill directories before loading them.
4. Run `econ-studio doctor --strict` before major work.
5. Use `econ-studio data-audit` before running models.
6. Use `econ-studio ledger`, `econ-studio claim-audit`, `econ-studio verify`, and `econ-studio paper audit` before claiming readiness.
7. Do not fabricate citations, data results, Stata/R output, or manuscript edits.
8. If a linked skill is unavailable, follow `docs/QUALITY_GATES.md` manually.
